# The dashboard's direct dependencies: what its code imports, plus the
# security floors below. requirements.txt is generated from this file and
# pins the whole tree; never edit it by hand. After changing this file, run
#
#     uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt --python-platform linux --python-version 3.13
#
# uv keeps every pin already in requirements.txt that still fits, so only
# what you changed moves; add `--upgrade-package <name>` to move one
# transitive. The tree is resolved for Linux on Python 3.13, which is what CI
# and the Docker image run. On Windows, pip also installs a few platform-only
# packages (colorama, pywin32) that are not pinned here. CI's
# "Dependency pins" job fails when requirements.txt is not exactly what this
# command produces, and the Docker build installs it with --no-deps.
